Found in `CharacterBuilder.jsx:169,253`, `DirectorSection.jsx:122`, `PromptOutput.jsx:47,50,355,358,367,370`.

If the component unmounts before the timer fires, the callback still runs and tries to set state on an unmounted component.

**Fix pattern** (apply to all instances):
```jsx
// Before:
setTimeout(() => setFlash(''), 1300);

// After:
useEffect(() => {
  if (!flash) return;
  const id = setTimeout(() => setFlash(''), 1300);
  return () => clearTimeout(id);
}, [flash]);
```

Or as a one-liner inside a click handler:
```jsx
const timerRef = useRef(null);
// in handler:
clearTimeout(timerRef.current);
timerRef.current = setTimeout(() => setCopiedSeedIdx(null), 1500);
// in cleanup:
useEffect(() => () => clearTimeout(timerRef.current), []);
```

---

**`App.jsx:294-301`** — `bankCharsForSelector.map()` creates new object references on every render, invalidating downstream memoization.

```jsx
// Before (creates new objects every render):
const derived = bankCharsForSelector.map(c => ({ ...c, extra: compute(c) }));

// After:
const derived = useMemo(
  () => bankCharsForSelector.map(c => ({ ...c, extra: compute(c) })),
  [bankCharsForSelector]
);
```

---

**`App.jsx:318-346`** — Character hydration effect depends on both `bankCharsForSelector` and `chars`, running on every unrelated character change.

```jsx
// Before: one effect doing too much
useEffect(() => {
  const lookup = new Map(bankCharsForSelector.map(c => [c.slug, c]));
  // ...hydrate slots using chars and lookup
}, [bankCharsForSelector, chars]);

// After: split into two effects with tighter scope
const bankLookup = useMemo(
  () => new Map(bankCharsForSelector.map(c => [c.slug, c])),
  [bankCharsForSelector]
);

useEffect(() => {
  // hydration logic using bankLookup and chars
}, [bankLookup, chars]);
```

**`App.jsx:533`** — `pendingApply` effect captures 6 dependencies including stable function refs. Wrap `captureApplyState` in `useCallback` so it's stable:
```jsx
const captureApplyState = useCallback(() => {
  return { scene, selectedDir, narrativeBeat, chips };
}, [scene, selectedDir, narrativeBeat, chips]);
```

---

**`App.jsx:307`** — `fetchBankSlugs()` called on every `activeTab` change with no cache.

```jsx
const bankSlugsCache = useRef(null);

const fetchBankSlugs = useCallback(async () => {
  if (bankSlugsCache.current) return bankSlugsCache.current;
  const result = await api.getBankSlugs();
  bankSlugsCache.current = result;
  return result;
}, []);
```

**`PromptOutput.jsx:176-200`** — Health check re-runs on every dependency change. Debounce it:
```jsx
useEffect(() => {
  const id = setTimeout(() => checkHealth(), 30_000);
  return () => clearTimeout(id);
}, [endpoint]); // only re-check when endpoint changes, not on every render
```

---

`JSON.stringify` is called on every chip group comparison in `summarizeApplyDiff`. For chip maps with many keys, this is expensive in a hot path.

```js
// Before:
if (JSON.stringify(bv) !== JSON.stringify(av)) { ... }

// After: compare keys+values structurally first
function shallowEqualSets(a, b) {
  if (a.size !== b.size) return false;
  for (const [k, v] of a) if (b.get(k) !== v) return false;
  return true;
}
// Only fall back to JSON.stringify for nested objects
```

---

Height recalculation triggers a synchronous browser layout on every `displayText` keystroke.

```jsx
// Before: fires on every character typed
useEffect(() => {
  ta.style.height = 'auto';
  ta.style.height = ta.scrollHeight + 'px';
}, [displayText]);

// After: debounce at ~16ms (one frame)
useEffect(() => {
  const id = requestAnimationFrame(() => {
    ta.style.height = 'auto';
    ta.style.height = ta.scrollHeight + 'px';
  });
  return () => cancelAnimationFrame(id);
}, [displayText]);
```

